  "planning_notes": [
    "Board is arduino:avr:uno; wiring pins preserved exactly as given: DHT11 on D7; heater relay D10; fan D5; buzzer D6; button D2; TM1637 CLK D4 and DIO D3; status LED D13.",
    "DHT sensor model assumed DHT11 because original requirement says DHT11; both temperature and humidity share pin D7 and have a shared validity request dht_valid on the same pin.",
    "TM1637 display operation is represented as a single program-owned tm1637_number output; how the model encodes 'setting value view mode' and 'current value view mode' into the displayed integer is a SysML/model decision.",
    "Serial output: requirement states '串口输出 incubation abnormal' but does not specify whether it is fixed text, a numeric/status code, and exact formatting. To avoid inventing the protocol, this proposal provides a typed boolean report gated by the abnormal condition; if fixed exact text is required, replace/augment with serial_text_output using that fixed string (format assumption otherwise cannot be guaranteed).",
    "Button electrical polarity (active-high vs active-low) is not specified. The proposal uses the catalog default by not overriding active_high/pullup; the model should treat the boolean as 'pressed=true' according to actual hardware polarity.",
    "Control_period_ms selected as 10ms as a reasonable scheduling granularity; actual reporting cadence, ventilation periodicity, and 1-minute threshold logic are implemented in the SysML model using elapsed_ms."
  ],
